WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.862 --> 00:00:10.570 line:84%
WILF BLACKBURN: It was important for me as a new leader
to make it clear what I stood for by what I was doing.

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:17.410 line:84%
But adding this third leg of
customer-centricity was a big, big step for us.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:20.440 line:90%
And it takes time for the results to become visible.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:21.700 line:90%
But I needed some action.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:29.059 line:84%
And so I was quite fortunate because....in a collaborative
way in which we were working -- offices were coming down,

00:00:29.059 --> 00:00:30.100 line:90%
walls were coming down --

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.310 line:90%
I no longer needed an office on the top floor.

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:39.970 line:84%
And we have a customer servicing center where we have
walk-in customers on the ground floor and nine desks.

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:46.885 line:84%
And so I've inhabited desk number
nine in the customer service center.

00:00:46.885 --> 00:00:51.430 line:84%
Of course, I don't do any customer servicing, but
there was a strong message to the organization

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:54.600 line:90%
that the customer is important to this CEO.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:03.710 line:84%
And that's really resonated, particularly in an organization
like ours, it's quite traditional, quite hierarchical,

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:09.070 line:84%
where senior executives in many
ways, including physically, often

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:12.160 line:84%
get positioned where they're a long,
long way from the real customers.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:19.270 line:84%
My first day with my seat being in the customer service
center -- well, it was a big day for me, but it was a much,

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:21.640 line:90%
much bigger day for our staff who worked there.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:28.760 line:84%
We have about 20 people who, in shifts, had been working
there; some of them had been there for about 20 years.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:33.490 line:84%
And in fact, the majority of them
been there for more than 15 years.

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:38.104 line:84%
And so to have the CEO coming and
sitting among them was a big thing.

00:01:38.104 --> 00:01:43.270 line:84%
I remember meeting them for breakfast before they started work
on the first day, and they were all quite nervous, of course.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:46.820 line:90%
And wondering, you know, am I there to keep an eye on them.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:53.170 line:84%
And it was some time before they realized that
actually I'm not there to check up on them.

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:58.330 line:84%
I'm there partly for symbolic
purpose, but also really to understand

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:01.285 line:90%
what the customer interactions are like, what happens.

00:02:01.285 --> 00:02:08.530 line:84%
And the staff relaxed when they would see
our agents, our financial consultants.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:10.539 line:90%
Often they would bring their customer.

00:02:10.539 --> 00:02:13.960 line:84%
But the agents would recognize me, and
say, "Oh Wilf, what are you doing here?"

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.060 line:90%
And then they'd introduce me to their customers.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:25.405 line:84%
And then our staff started to relax, where they could see the
real value was in the interest it was creating for customers,

00:02:25.405 --> 00:02:28.090 line:90%
and for our financial consultants.

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:32.590 line:84%
And also the interest for me was to find out
what's the customer experience really like.

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:39.375 line:84%
So then it was more powerful for many of our other
staff to see the CEO didn't need a big office,

00:02:39.375 --> 00:02:45.240 line:90%
and the CEO wanted to be where the customers were.

